WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:11.640
66. Paul Gauguin. Paul Gauguin was a French artist who is now seen as one of the founders

2
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:18.920
of modern art. He began painting as an impressionist, but he grew tired of that style. He evolved

3
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:24.600
toward the use of figures and clear, outlined blocks of color. Indeed, he is best known

4
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:31.280
for his use of flat color. He used images and symbols from his travels in exotic lands,

5
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:38.720
such as Martinique, Panama, and Tahiti, giving his paintings a sense of mystery. Gauguin lived

6
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:45.360
in Europe for most of his early life. He married a Dutch woman and had five children with her.

7
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:51.460
But he left European styles behind early in his art career. He grew tired of classical

8
00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:58.440
European perspective and subtle coloring. Influenced by Japanese prints and folk art,

9
00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:05.560
he began to move towards Closinism. Closinism is a painting style named after a glass technique

10
00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:11.700
in which colored glass is put into blocks or cells to create a picture. Closinism painting

11
00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:17.840
uses bold colors and black outlines to define objects clearly. Gauguin's painting, The

12
00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:25.340
Yellow Christ, is considered the greatest example of a Closinist work. In 1891, a frustrated

13
00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:32.040
Gauguin left Europe and sailed to the tropics. He lived most of the rest of his life in Polynesia.

14
00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:36.880
He painted many of his most famous works there, including Where Do We Come From?, What Are

15
00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:42.420
We?, Where Are We Going?, which many believe to be his masterpiece. His works from this

16
00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:49.000
time in his life depict Polynesian life, usually from a biased point of view that shows Polynesia

17
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:55.360
as a paradise, and also use a variety of religious symbols. Gauguin may not have had

18
00:01:55.360 --> 00:02:01.640
a conventionally successful life. He never made much money, and his family fell apart.

19
00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:08.120
However, the distance he put between himself and his culture certainly paid off in his art.
